## How it works

Before: `btn_clk → debug → purchase`

```python
stream.edit_events(rename={"btn_clk": "button_click"}, delete=["debug"])
```

After — renaming and deleting happen in the same pass, so you only walk the
unique event list once:

`button_click → purchase`

Renaming an event to a name that already exists merges the two. Events absent
from `rename` are left alone; use [`drop_events`](/docs/data-processors/drop-events)
or [`rename_events`](/docs/data-processors/rename-events) when you only need one
of the two operations.

